      "text": "We have the product of the first n terms of the sequence $\\frac{1}{n} \\cdot \\frac{2}{n+1} \\cdot \\frac{3}{n+2} \\cdots \\frac{n}{n+1}$. In this case, n=49, so we have $\\frac{1}{49} \\cdot \\frac{2}{50} \\cdot \\frac{3}{51} \\cdots \\frac{49}{52}$. Since $n = 50$, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by 50 to get $\\frac{50!}{50 \\cdot 51 \\cdots 52} = \\frac{50!}{50 \\cdot 51 \\cdot 52 \\cdot 53} = \\frac{1}{53}$.The answer is: 53",
